{{!
    @template local_moodesk/shell/topbar

    Application-shell top bar: navigation toggle (left), then notifications and
    the user menu (right). Search and the app-grid from the design mockups are
    intentionally omitted (no backend / would be a new feature).

    Notifications and the user menu surface Moodle chrome the embedded layout
    removes — they re-expose Moodle's own notification stream and account links,
    not new data. The user menu is a native <details>/<summary> disclosure;
    app_shell.js enhances it with outside-click / Escape close + ARIA.

    Context variables:
      * togglelabel   - Accessible label for the navigation toggle
      * notifications - {url, label, hascount, countlabel}
      * user          - {fullname, rolelabel, avatar (html), menulabel,
                         profileurl, profilelabel, preferencesurl,
                         preferenceslabel, logouturl, logoutlabel}

    Example context (json):
    {
      "togglelabel": "Toggle navigation",
      "notifications": {
        "url": "/message/output/popup/notifications.php",
        "label": "Notifications",
        "hascount": true,
        "countlabel": "3"
      },
      "user": {
        "fullname": "Ada Lovelace",
        "rolelabel": "Agent",
        "avatar": "<span class=\"userpicture\"></span>",
        "menulabel": "User menu",
        "profileurl": "/user/profile.php",
        "profilelabel": "Profile",
        "preferencesurl": "/user/preferences.php",
        "preferenceslabel": "Preferences",
        "logouturl": "/login/logout.php",
        "logoutlabel": "Log out"
      }
    }
}}
<header class="moodesk-app__topbar">

    {{! aria-controls is applied by app_shell.js once the sidebar is in the DOM.
        Hardcoding it here makes this partial invalid on its own — the target
        lives in the sidebar partial, which the mustache linter renders
        separately. }}
    <button type="button" class="moodesk-app__nav-toggle" data-region="moodesk-nav-toggle" data-controls="moodesk-app-sidebar" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="{{togglelabel}}">
        <svg class="moodesk-app__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#mhd-icon-menu"></use></svg>
    </button>

    <div class="moodesk-app__topbar-spacer"></div>

    <a class="moodesk-app__notif" href="{{notifications.url}}" aria-label="{{notifications.label}}">
        <svg class="moodesk-app__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#mhd-icon-bell"></use></svg>
        {{#notifications.hascount}}<span class="moodesk-app__notif-badge" aria-hidden="true">{{notifications.countlabel}}</span>{{/notifications.hascount}}
    </a>

    <details class="moodesk-app__usermenu" data-region="moodesk-usermenu">
        <summary class="moodesk-app__user" role="button" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="{{user.menulabel}}">
            <span class="moodesk-app__user-info">
                <span class="moodesk-app__user-name">{{user.fullname}}</span>
                {{#user.rolelabel}}<span class="moodesk-app__user-role">{{user.rolelabel}}</span>{{/user.rolelabel}}
            </span>
            <span class="moodesk-app__user-avatar">{{{user.avatar}}}</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="moodesk-app__usermenu-panel" role="menu">
            <a class="moodesk-app__usermenu-item" role="menuitem" href="{{user.profileurl}}">{{user.profilelabel}}</a>
            <a class="moodesk-app__usermenu-item" role="menuitem" href="{{user.preferencesurl}}">{{user.preferenceslabel}}</a>
            <a class="moodesk-app__usermenu-item" role="menuitem" href="{{user.logouturl}}">{{user.logoutlabel}}</a>
        </div>
    </details>

</header>
